IO-55: track and report the time a pump runs off its curve

The Pumping Summary printed 0.0 in both "% Time Off Pump Curve" columns
for every pump. Mark the pump's flow class in computePumpFlowK() as legacy
pump_getInflow() does (DN_DRY when the curve variable - wet-well volume,
depth or head - is below the curve's first point, UP_DRY when it is above
the last), add the running time in each state to two new LinkData
counters, and print them as a percentage of the pump's running time.

Requires: IO-54

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-54_swmm600.patch IO-55_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 4bd96d2..3acb5d5 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -5447,6 +5447,12 @@ void SWMMEngine::updateStatistics(double dt_routing) noexcept {
                 // (q > MIN_RUNOFF_FLOW, stats.c)
                 double& qmin = ctx_.links.stat_pump_min_flow[uj];
                 if (q > 0.001 && (qmin == 0.0 || q < qmin)) qmin = q;
+                // off-curve time as marked by computePumpFlowK(), over the
+                // same steps (legacy stats_updateLinkStats)
+                if (q > 0.001 && ctx_.links.flow_class[uj] == FlowClass::DN_DRY)
+                    ctx_.links.stat_pump_off_curve_low[uj] += dt_routing;
+                if (q > 0.001 && ctx_.links.flow_class[uj] == FlowClass::UP_DRY)
+                    ctx_.links.stat_pump_off_curve_high[uj] += dt_routing;
 
                 // Pump energy (kWh), matching legacy link_getPower:
                 //   power_kW = |dh| * |q| / 8.814 * KWperHP ; energy += power_kW * dt/3600
